    # 1. Immediately returns control to the caller (corix init), fixing the blocking issue.
    # 2. Creates a new process independent of the parent shell, so it won't exit when the terminal closes.
    # 3. The inner while loop inherits the "never-exit" nature, responsible for monitoring and restarting the Python process.
    (
